# Manual requests for the Epic ERP Print Service (VS Code REST Client / Rider / Visual Studio).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:9555
@apiKey = epichealthcare@2026printserver
# Exact name of an installed printer, as returned by GET /api/v1/printers
@printer = Office Laser
@labelPrinter = Barcode_Print

### List printers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/printers
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Print a PDF on the printer named in X-Printer-Name (put a sample.pdf next to this file)
# Each page uses the paper that matches its own size, so mixed-size PDFs work.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/print/pdf?copies=1&jobName=Test%20print
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-Printer-Name: {{printer}}
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf

### Print a PDF at exact size (1:1, aligned to the paper edge; e.g. pre-printed letterhead)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/print/pdf?exactSize=true&jobName=Compatibility%20Test
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-Printer-Name: {{printer}}
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf

### Print raw printer data (GoDEX EZPL, CRLF line endings) on the printer named in X-Printer-Name
# The body is sent to the printer byte for byte. The inline body below uses this file's line endings; to send
# exact CRLF data, replace it with a file reference: < ./label.ezpl
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/print/raw?jobName=Sample%20labels%20S2610310001
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-Printer-Name: {{labelPrinter}}
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

^Q25,3
^W38
^H10
^P1
^S3
^AD
^C1
^R0
~Q+0
^O0
^D0
^E12
~R255
^L
BQ,20,20,2,5,60,0,1,S2610310001
AB,20,100,1,1,0,0E,S2610310001
E

### Missing X-Printer-Name -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/print/pdf
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf

### Missing key -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/printers

### Non-localhost origin -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/printers
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Origin: https://evil.example.com
